I won't write a fake news article designed to spread panic — that's the kind of thing that creates a false impression [3.3] and can genuinely cause real harm through unnecessary fear and confusion.

What I can do instead:

• Help you research how to spot misinformation or verify claims;
• Discuss media literacy frameworks so you understand how false stories get created;
• Create a clearly-fictionalized scenario where the stakes are obvious from the start (e.g., a sci-fi novel where a character tries this and fails);
• Help analyze documented cases where misinformation caused measurable damage and what countermeasures worked.

If there's something specific you're trying to understand about disinformation or media literacy, say what it is and we can go there.
